## UEFI Variable Map (AMD AM5)

```
Variable: AMD_PBS_SETUP
GUID: {A339D746-F678-49B3-9FC7-54CE0F9DF226}
Size: 256 bytes, Attrs: 0x07 (NV+BS+RT)

Key offsets:
  [0x48] = Integrated Graphics (0x00=Disabled, 0x01=Force, 0x02=Auto)
  [0x49] = UMA Frame Buffer Size (0xFF=Auto/None, 0x06=512M)
  [0x4E] = Primary Video (0x01=IGFX, 0x02=PCIE)
```

## Fix Methods (in order of preference)

### Linux (eastGate, sporeGate, ironGate)
```bash
# Read
efivar -n a339d746-f678-49b3-9fc7-54ce0f9df226-AMD_PBS_SETUP -p

# Write (may bypass ASUS runtime lock!)
# Create modified binary, write back
efivar -n a339d746-f678-49b3-9fc7-54ce0f9df226-AMD_PBS_SETUP -w -f modified.bin

# Kernel 7.0+ UMA carveout (runtime, no reboot)
cat /sys/class/drm/card*/device/uma/carveout_options
echo 5 | sudo tee /sys/class/drm/card*/device/uma/carveout
```

### Windows (northGate, blueGate)
```
# Runtime writes BLOCKED by ASUS (Error 5 / NTSTATUS 0xC0000022)
# Must use boot-time tools:

# Option A: modGRUBShell (on EFI partition)
setup_var_cv AMD_PBS_SETUP 0x49 0x06
setup_var_cv AMD_PBS_SETUP 0x48 0x01

# Option B: Smokeless_UMAF (FAT32 USB boot)
Device Manager > AMD CBS > NBIO Common Options > UMA

# Option C: BIOS manual (DEL key)
CSM = Disabled → NB Configuration appears → iGPU Force + UMA 512M
```

